      <body>
         <ab>
            
            
            <persName type="reg">
               <forename>Carlo</forename> <surname>Linati</surname>
            </persName>
            <persName type="full">Carlo Linati</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1878-04-25"/>
            <date type="death" when="1949-12-11"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>
                    <p>Italian novelist, literary critic, translator, and co-founder of the Italian literary magazine <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Il Convegno</name>. A 1913 trip to Ireland led to Linati’s interest in Irish writers. His Italian translations of <name type="person" key="yeat65">Yeats</name> and Synge caught the attention of JJ, who in 1918 invited him to translate <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>. Although this never materialized, his translation of Exiles appeared in three numbers of Il Convegno in 1920 and of the story “Araby” in that magazine in 1924. In September of 1920, JJ sent him a “schema” outlining elements of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Ulysses</name>. In 1926 the same magazine published an excerpt from Ulysses translated by Linati. Linati’s translation of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Stephen Hero</name> appeared in 1950.<hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                    </p>

                    
                </p>
         </div>
